Late September is typically cooler than late August in this region (seasonal cooling). So temperature on Sept 27 being higher than Aug 28 is less likely than not, roughly 25-35%.

The two stations are geographically close (~100km apart, similar climate), so their day-to-day temperatures are highly correlated. This means B given A should be much higher than baseline.

